<DocsLayout title="Mod compatibility" description="How etmc works alongside other mods.">
  <p>
    etmc only changes how the connection travels. It doesn't touch Minecraft's packets, so to the game and your
    other mods it's a normal server connection.
  </p>

  <h2>ViaFabricPlus</h2>
  <p>
    etmc works with ViaFabricPlus, including its automatic version detection, with nothing to set up. etmc doesn't
    require it.
  </p>
  <p>
    To keep a version you've forced in ViaFabricPlus between sessions when you join from a config URL, set
    <code>joinLocalPort</code> in <code>config/etmc.json</code> to a fixed port. ViaFabricPlus saves its settings
    per address, and etmc otherwise picks a new port each time.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
